  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 315 AM CDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\nThe end of the relentless heat is in sight. Behind the front\ntemperatures are expected to be much cooler. For Tuesday and\nWednesday, NBM guidance shows that high temperatures will be in\nthe low to mid 70s, with the northern portions of the area\npossibly staying in the upper 60s for their high temperatures\n(60-80% chance). Low temperatures will also dip into the 50s.\nThis air mass will continue to dominate for the rest of the week\nwith a gradual warming through the 70s, reaching the low 80s by\nnext weekend.\n\nThe GFS and ECMWF both show a mid-level ridge building over the\nGreat Lakes and into the southeastern Canada region with a\ncenter of low pressure over the Ohio Valley by mid week. The\nridge should remain fairly stationary over southeastern Canada,\nwhile the low pressure center will slowly move to the east coast\nof the CONUS. This pattern will allow for continued westerly and\nnorthwesterly flow to help moderate our temperatures into next\nweekend and limit the moisture transported into the region,\npreventing another return of the heat and humidity this week.",
